NAME
    awk - select records and print bounded fields

SYNOPSIS
    awk [-F SEP] PROGRAM [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Splits records on ASCII whitespace, or on the one-byte SEP supplied by -F.
    Actions use { print ITEM, ... }, where an item is $0 through $32, NR, NF,
    or a quoted literal. A missing action prints the complete record.

    Supported selectors are /LITERAL/ and $N == "LITERAL". Patterns are
    literal bytes. Variables, arithmetic, regular expressions, BEGIN/END,
    assignments, functions, and general awk expressions are not implemented.
